#* {{quote-text|enm|year=1395|author=[[w:Wycliffe bible|Wycliffe Bible]]|url=http://www.studylight.org/desk/index.cgi?t1=en_wyc&q1=Romans%202|title=Romans 2:4
|passage=Whether `dispisist thou the richessis of his goodnesse, and the pacience, and the long abidyng? Knowist thou not, that the benygnyte of God '''ledith''' thee to forthenkyng?}}
#* {{quote-text|enm|year=1395|author=Wycliffe Bible|url=http://www.studylight.org/desk/index.cgi?t1=en_wyc&q1=2%20Chronicles%2025|title=II Chronicles 25:11
|passage=Forsothe Amasie '''ledde''' out tristili his puple, and yede in to the valei of makyngis of salt, and he killide of the sones of Seir ten thousynde.}}
